body:
> Currently, useParams() will only return string, there is no return array logic.
> Should we add return array logic?

@JuniorTour The expectation is an array according to the return type (`string | string[]`) & the docs... Its also a bit odd it'd be different from the `params` prop on layout/page's

For the time being I wrote a small conditional that will make sure catch all routes can be used in edge runtime. Locally, the correct string array is returned `['path1', 'path2']`, but once deployed it will look like this: `['path1%2Fpath2']`. I just split the single string in the array on the delimiter to make it an array again.

```export default async function Page({ params }: { params: { slug: string[] } }) {
  const urlParams = params;
  
  if (params.slug.length === 1 && params.slug[0].includes("%2F")) {
    urlParams["slug"] = params.slug[0].split("%2F");
  }
  ```

I just ran into the same issue in the latest version (13.4.9), albeit with an async server component instead of the `useParams` hook. The code looks like:

```typescript
export const generateMetadata = async ({
  params: { categories },
}: {
  params: { categories: string[] };
}):
  console.log(categories);
```

In dev, `categories` is an array of strings as expected, but on vercel with edge runtime enabled it is a url-encoded string.
